# Day 36

**31km / 9.5 hours**

Today taught me I am certainly not invincible. I started early from the hut hoping for a nice sunrise but it was still mostly obscured by clouds. After leaving the hut there was some traversing to a nearby summit before dropping down for a few hundred metres. Even though this section was only 6km or so it was marked as 3-5 hours on the sign which would've been because of the mud and steep sections requiring extra care and slowing progress down immensely. It ended up taking me around 2.5 hours but I was going a little quicker than normal I think. 

![The view from a lookout when the clouds moved aside for a bit](./view.avif)

After that it was back to the road for a while. Not much to say about this, there was some road works going on which I had to skirt past and have brief chats with the crew fixing up the road. Other than this it was just quiet roads until the farmland. However by this point I had a problem, my socks were wet and had holes in them which caused my right foot to start to hurt from blisters. I tried to use plasters to patch it up to keep going but it still didn't feel comfortable. Still nothing for it but to soldier on.

![A nice part of the forest to walk through, definitely a pleasant atmosphere](./forest-path.avif)

I struggled onwards frustrated with my foot since everything else was coping okay. It made progress slower as I wasn't walking freely but it wasn't unbearable, just irritating. After what seemed like forever I got to the shelter I could stay at, it was a converted barn and much appreciated. Hopefully my foot will be better tomorrow but this is definitely a sign in favour of taking some time off soon.